        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/r/j/trent-bridge-wp/first-day-of-the-2010-england-.jpg",
          "filename": "First day of the 2010 England-Pakistan Test Match - geograph.org.uk - 1986155.jpg",
          "caption": "First day of the 2010 England-Pakistan Test Match, near to West Bridgford, Nottinghamshire, Great Britain.\nThe score is 306-4 late in the day. Eoin Morgan has reached a maiden Test century and is on 113 not out as he leaves a ball from Mohammad Asif alone outside the off stump. Paul Collingwood (71 not out) is the non-striker. The photograph was taken from the middle tier of the Radcliffe Road Stand, where I was enjoying my birthday and feeling glad I wasn't the lonely TV cameraman on the boom lift high above the pavilion.",
          "alt": "First day of the 2010 England-Pakistan Test Match, near to West Bridgford, Nottinghamshire, Great Britain.\nThe score is 306-4 late in the day. Eoin Morgan has reached a maiden Test century and is on 113 not out as he leaves a ball from Mohammad Asif alone outside the off stump. Paul Collingwood (71 not out) is the non-striker. The photograph was taken from the middle tier of the Radcliffe Road Stand, where I was enjoying my birthday and feeling glad I wasn't the lonely TV cameraman on the boom lift high above the pavilion.",
